<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged and movement was slow, dealers in the central U.S. High Plains said Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers in Oklahoma and Kansas said clear weather conditions had enabled fields to dry out during the weekend. But dealers warned that more rains were forecast for this week, which could delay harvesting of corn and sorghum as well as planting of HRW wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;If we don't get any rain, I'd say there's going to be some haevy plantings this week,&quot; a northern Oklahoma dealer said.  </p>
